---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { siteFromHost } from '../../content';
const site = siteFromHost();
const path = '/compare/activecampaign-vs-klaviyo';
const title = 'ActiveCampaign vs Klaviyo for Shopify SMS and Email: 2026 Comparison';
const description = 'A strict ActiveCampaign vs Klaviyo comparison for Shopify: email and SMS depth, segmentation, pricing, consent, workflow pilots, and operational fit.';
const faqs = [
  { question: 'Which is better for Shopify SMS?', answer: 'Klaviyo is generally the stronger choice when SMS is tied closely to Shopify product, order, and behavioral data. ActiveCampaign is stronger when CRM stages, sales follow-up, and cross-channel automation matter more than commerce-native depth. Verify current SMS features, consent controls, and regional availability before committing.' },
  { question: 'Which is better for Shopify email?', answer: 'Klaviyo fits stores that need deep catalog and event segmentation. ActiveCampaign fits teams that need broader CRM-linked branching and sales automation. Run the same welcome, cart, post-purchase, replenishment, and win-back tests in both.' },
  { question: 'How should pricing be compared?', answer: 'Model active profiles or contacts, email sends, SMS volume, seats, feature tiers, and seasonal peaks for twelve months. The cheaper starting plan is not necessarily cheaper once the store runs the required workflows.' },
  { question: 'Can a store use both?', answer: 'It can, but shared ownership must be explicit. Decide which platform sends each email and SMS job, synchronize consent and purchase suppression, and prevent duplicate cart or post-purchase touches.' },
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={description} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="py-14 md:py-20"><div class="container max-w-5xl"><nav class="mb-8 text-sm"><a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a><span class="mx-2">/</span><span>ActiveCampaign vs Klaviyo</span></nav>
    <header class="max-w-4xl"><p class="editorial-kicker">Head-to-head · Shopify email and SMS</p><h1 class="hero-title mt-5">ActiveCampaign vs Klaviyo for Shopify</h1><p class="mt-7 text-xl leading-9 text-slate-700">Both platforms can appear in a Shopify SMS shortlist, but they begin from different centers of gravity. ActiveCampaign is CRM and automation first; Klaviyo is commerce data and retention first. The right choice depends on whether the store’s hardest problem is account-aware branching or product-and-order-aware messaging.</p><p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-700">This page evaluates the pair through consent, catalog events, cart recovery, post-purchase timing, replenishment, win-back, reporting, and the operator time required to safely change a journey before a launch.</p></header>
    <div class="mt-10 card overflow-x-auto"><h2 class="px-5 py-4 font-serif text-2xl font-black text-slate-950">Comparison at a glance</h2><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>ActiveCampaign</th><th>Klaviyo</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Core strength</td><td>CRM-linked branching and sales automation</td><td>Shopify events, catalog, segmentation, and retention</td></tr><tr><td>SMS fit</td><td>Useful when SMS is part of a wider automation</td><td>Useful when SMS needs commerce behavior and product context</td></tr><tr><td>Cart recovery</td><td>Conditional logic and account-aware follow-up</td><td>Deep behavioral and catalog segmentation</td></tr><tr><td>Pricing lens</td><td>Contacts, tier, seats, and features</td><td>Active profiles, sends, SMS, and features</td></tr><tr><td>Main risk</td><td>CRM complexity for a pure ecommerce team</td><td>Profile growth and operational complexity at scale</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
    <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl"><h2>ActiveCampaign’s strongest Shopify use case</h2><p>ActiveCampaign makes the most sense when a Shopify store has more than a consumer lifecycle. Wholesale inquiries, sales-assisted accounts, membership stages, and manual follow-up can share a record with marketing automation. A cart reminder can branch by account status instead of applying the same discount to every buyer.</p><p>That flexibility requires governance. Define identity, consent, purchase exits, SMS permissions, and the owner of every branch before adding more conditions. ActiveCampaign is powerful when the team will maintain the system; it is expensive operationally when no one owns the data model.</p><h2>Klaviyo’s strongest Shopify use case</h2><p>Klaviyo is strongest when product, catalog, browse, order, and customer behavior should shape the next email or text. A replenishment flow can use product-specific timing, a VIP message can reflect value and category, and a cart flow can distinguish a first-time buyer from a repeat customer without building a separate CRM process.</p><p>The trade-off is profile and channel discipline. More event depth creates more opportunities for stale data, duplicate flows, and rising profile cost. Review event freshness, consent source, frequency caps, and purchaser suppression before expanding beyond the first few journeys.</p><h2>SMS workflow test</h2><p>Test a cart flow with a customer opted into SMS and email. The first message should solve an objection without assuming a discount. Verify quiet hours, STOP handling, channel preference, and suppression after purchase. Then compare incremental contribution, not the dashboard’s combined attributed revenue.</p><table><thead><tr><th>SMS check</th><th>ActiveCampaign question</th><th>Klaviyo question</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Consent</td><td>Is SMS permission stored separately from email?</td><td>Is consent source and region available to the flow?</td></tr><tr><td>Collision</td><td>Can CRM and cart branches share one frequency rule?</td><td>Can email and SMS share a clear priority and cap?</td></tr><tr><td>Purchase exit</td><td>How quickly does the order event stop the journey?</td><td>Does the purchaser event suppress every related message?</td></tr><tr><td>Reporting</td><td>Can sales-assisted outcomes be separated from SMS?</td><td>Can incremental margin be tested against a holdout?</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>Email workflow test</h2><p>Rebuild welcome, cart, post-purchase, replenishment, and win-back in both platforms with the same audience rules. Score setup time, event accuracy, edit safety, purchaser suppression, and reporting. A platform that produces a higher attributed number but cannot explain who received which channel is not the winner.</p><h2>Pricing and total cost</h2><p>Build a twelve-month model with contacts or profiles, email sends, SMS volume, seats, implementation time, and peak-season growth. ActiveCampaign can justify its cost when CRM handoffs change conversion or productivity. Klaviyo can justify its cost when catalog and behavioral segmentation produce measurable incremental retention. Include discount margin and support load in both cases.</p><h2>Who should choose which?</h2><p><strong>Choose ActiveCampaign</strong> when CRM stages, sales follow-up, B2B or membership logic, and flexible branching are load-bearing. <strong>Choose Klaviyo</strong> when Shopify data depth, product-aware segmentation, and coordinated email/SMS retention are load-bearing.</p><p><strong>Use both only with a written ownership map.</strong> Assign each welcome, cart, post-purchase, replenishment, win-back, and promotional job to one sender. Synchronize consent, order ID, purchase state, and suppression before peak season.</p><h2>90-day pilot</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Phase</th><th>Test</th><th>Evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Weeks 1–2</td><td>Consent, identity, event and purchase exits</td><td>Inbox timeline with zero duplicate sends</td></tr><tr><td>Weeks 3–6</td><td>Cart and post-purchase journeys</td><td>Incremental contribution and complaint rate</td></tr><tr><td>Weeks 7–12</td><td>Replenishment, win-back, and peak edit</td><td>Maintenance time, margin, and repeat order</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>Verdict</h2><p>ActiveCampaign wins when Shopify lifecycle work must share a CRM and sales process. Klaviyo wins when commerce data and coordinated email/SMS retention are the priority. Choose from the five-workflow pilot, not from a generic “best Shopify SMS app” ranking.</p></article>
  </div></section><FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="ActiveCampaign vs Klaviyo FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
